From 0585158dbf878b7f594bc5a7ca400e5eb3187684 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 05:42:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Phase 4a: per-store fulfilment toggles (dine-in / takeaway /
 reservations)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Each store now offers only the order types it should. locations.js resolves a
per-store fulfilment {dineIn,takeaway,reservations}: an explicit per-store toggle
wins, else a default from the store type — Physical = all three, Pop-up =
takeaway only, Event = dine-in/booths only. (The 'event' type is recognised now;
its free/no-payment ordering lands in the next phase.)

- publicList() exposes each store's fulfilment.
- OrderTypeBar shows only the allowed choices, and when a store offers a single
  order type it drops the segmented toggle and goes straight to that flow (a
  takeaway-only pop-up lands directly on the takeaway timing).
- App keeps the selected order type valid when you switch stores (a stale
  'Dine in' can't persist onto a takeaway-only pop-up).
- Admin Locations: 'Order types offered at this store' checkboxes per store,
  defaulting to the type's defaults and overridable — so a pop-up CAN switch on
  dine-in/tables for a booth setup.

Backward compatible: a single-site deploy (and any store with no overrides) keeps
all three order types.
